shoestring-wm is a lightweight Rust Wayland window manager built on
Smithay, shipped with its companion tools: a status bar, dmenu-style
launcher, notification daemon, screen locker, screenshot and region
pickers, a confirmation helper, and an IPC control client.

It targets a low-dependency desktop and exposes a Unix-socket JSON IPC
so the running compositor can be queried, scripted, and automated. Once
installed it appears in the display manager's session menu; pick
"shoestring-wm" at the login screen and log in.
